"
I am the abstract superclass of the tests that run the class-side methods having a pragma, one test per method.

The design is modular: I check nothing myself, and each package (or project) gets its own copy of `ReScriptMethodsTest` and `ReSampleInstanceMethodsTest`, made with the script shown below in Public API and Key Messages (`copyNamed:forPackagesNamed:in:`). The copy lives in the tests of that package, checks only its packages, and depends only on `SUnit-Core`, so the package does not have to load mine.

## Responsibility:

- Find the class-side methods with my pragma (`pragmaSelector`) in the packages to check, except the excluded ones.
- Run each of them, closing the windows it opens.
- Make a copy of my subclass for a project (`copyNamed:forPackagesNamed:in:`), which depends only on `SUnit-Core`.

## Collaborators:

- `ParametrizedTestCase` and `ParametrizedTestMatrix`: give each test one method (`method`).
- `ReScriptMethodsTest` and `ReSampleInstanceMethodsTest`: my subclasses, for `<script>` and `<sampleInstance>`.
- `Package`: answers the methods of a package to check, extensions included.

## Public API and Key Messages

- Class side: `packageNamesToCheck` and `excludedMethods` (strings such as `'MyClass class>>#resetAll'`) are the hooks of a copy.
- Class side: `copyNamed: aSymbol forPackagesNamed: someNames in: aPackageName` installs a copy for a project. For example:

```
ReScriptMethodsTest
	copyNamed: #MyProjectScriptMethodsTest
	forPackagesNamed: #( 'MyProject-Core' 'MyProject-UI' )
	in: 'MyProject-Tests'
```

## Internal Representation

- `method`: the class-side method checked by this test, set by the test matrix.

### Implementation Points

- I am abstract and check no package: only copies are run.
- A test never passes while checking nothing: `setUp` fails when there is no package to check, when one of them is not loaded (naming it), or when no method has my pragma.
- A copy is a subclass of `ParametrizedTestCase` holding my methods and those of my subclass, except the class-side ones answered by `notCopiedSelectors`, which the copy defines itself.
- When there is no Morphic world, `closeWindowsOpenedDuring:` only runs its block. A method opening a modal dialog blocks the test: exclude it.
"
Class {
	#name : 'RePragmaMethodsTest',
	#superclass : 'ParametrizedTestCase',
	#instVars : [
		'method'
	],
	#category : 'General-Rules-Tests',
	#package : 'General-Rules-Tests'
}

{ #category : 'copying' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> copyNamed: aSymbol forPackagesNamed: someNames in: aPackageName [
	"Install and answer a copy of me named aSymbol in the package aPackageName, checking the packages named someNames. The copy is a subclass of ParametrizedTestCase holding all my methods and those of my superclasses, so that a project can run me without depending on my package."

	| copy |
	copy := ParametrizedTestCase << aSymbol
		slots: (self allInstVarNames copyWithoutAll: ParametrizedTestCase allInstVarNames);
		package: aPackageName;
		install.
	(self withAllSuperclasses copyUpTo: ParametrizedTestCase) reverseDo: [ :class |
		class methods do: [ :each | copy compile: each sourceCode classified: each protocolName ].
		class class methods do: [ :each |
			(self notCopiedSelectors includes: each selector) ifFalse: [
				copy class compile: each sourceCode classified: each protocolName ] ] ].
	copy class compile: ('isAbstract{1}{1}{2}^ false' format: { String cr. String tab }) classified: #private.
	copy class
		compile: ('packageNamesToCheck{1}{1}{2}^ {3}' format: { String cr. String tab. someNames asArray printString })
		classified: #accessing.
	copy comment: ('I am a copy of `{1}` checking the packages of a project. I was generated by `{1} class>>#copyNamed:forPackagesNamed:in:`; my class-side `packageNamesToCheck` and `excludedMethods` can be edited.' format: { self name }).
	^ copy
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> excludedMethods [
	"Answer the methods I do not run, as strings such as 'MyClass class>>#resetAll'. Override it in a copy to exclude methods that must not be run by a test."

	^ #(  )
]

{ #category : 'private' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> isAbstract [

	^ self == RePragmaMethodsTest
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> methodsToCheck [
	"Answer the class-side methods with my pragma in the packages to check, except the excluded ones."

	| packages |
	packages := (self packageNamesToCheck collect: [ :each | self packageOrganizer packageNamed: each ifAbsent: [ nil ] ]) reject: [ :each | each isNil ].
	^ ((packages flatCollect: [ :package |
		package methods select: [ :each | each methodClass isClassSide and: [ each hasPragmaNamed: self pragmaSelector ] ] ])
		reject: [ :each | self excludedMethods includes: each printString ]) asArray
		sort: [ :a :b | a printString <= b printString ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> missingPackageNames [
	"Answer the names of the packages to check that are not loaded."

	^ self packageNamesToCheck reject: [ :each | self packageOrganizer hasPackage: each ]
]

{ #category : 'copying' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> notCopiedSelectors [
	"Answer the class-side selectors a copy does not take from me: it defines its own."

	^ #( #isAbstract #packageNamesToCheck #notCopiedSelectors #copyNamed:forPackagesNamed:in: )
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> packageNamesToCheck [
	"Answer the names of the packages whose methods I check. A copy for a project answers the packages of the project."

	^ #(  )
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> pragmaSelector [
	"Answer the pragma of the class-side methods I check."

	^ self subclassResponsibility
]

{ #category : 'building suites' }
RePragmaMethodsTest class >> testParameters [
	"Answer one option per method to check, or an empty matrix when there is none: ParametrizedTestCase>>#setUp cannot use a matrix without options."

	| methods |
	methods := self methodsToCheck.
	methods ifEmpty: [ ^ ParametrizedTestMatrix new ].
	^ ParametrizedTestMatrix new
		forSelector: #method addOptions: methods;
		yourself
]

{ #category : 'running' }
RePragmaMethodsTest >> assertPackagesToCheckAreLoaded [
	"Fail when there is no package to check or when one of them is not loaded: a test checking nothing must not pass."

	| missing |
	self deny: self class packageNamesToCheck isEmpty description: 'No package to check'.
	missing := self class missingPackageNames.
	missing ifNotEmpty: [ self fail: ('Packages to check not loaded: {1}' format: { ', ' join: missing }) ]
]

{ #category : 'running' }
RePragmaMethodsTest >> closeWindowsOpenedDuring: aBlock [
	"Answer the value of aBlock, and close the windows and morphs it added to the world, if there is one."

	| world before |
	world := Smalltalk globals at: #World ifAbsent: [ ^ aBlock value ].
	before := world submorphs copy.
	^ aBlock ensure: [
		world submorphs
			reject: [ :each | before includes: each ]
			thenDo: [ :each | each delete ] ]
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest >> method [

	^ method
]

{ #category : 'accessing' }
RePragmaMethodsTest >> method: aCompiledMethod [

	method := aCompiledMethod
]

{ #category : 'running' }
RePragmaMethodsTest >> runMethod [
	"Answer the result of sending the selector of my method to its class, closing the windows it opens."

	^ self closeWindowsOpenedDuring: [ method methodClass instanceSide perform: method selector ]
]

{ #category : 'running' }
RePragmaMethodsTest >> setUp [

	super setUp.
	self assertPackagesToCheckAreLoaded.
	method ifNil: [ self fail: ('No class-side method with <{1}> in the packages to check' format: { self class pragmaSelector }) ]
]
